--- platform-capability note: why TEST_EXIT=1 (full solution) ---
The only failures in the full-solution `dotnet test` are the 147 tests in TeslaSync.App.UITests.
They are WinUI 3 UI-automation (WinAppDriver/Appium) end-to-end tests and fail — by the harness's
own intentional design (it fails rather than silently skips) — because the UI-automation runner is
absent on this headless runner. Verbatim probe evidence (TeslaSync.App.UITests.Fixtures.
UiAutomationUnavailableException):
  "UI automation cannot run: WinAppDriver/Appium runner is absent: nothing is listening on
   http://127.0.0.1:4723/ and WinAppDriver.exe was not found at its standard install paths or on PATH."
These tests are generic shell/navigation/state-matrix/a11y E2E checks (not specific to DrivingSection),
they are not part of this surface, and they fail identically on the untouched baseline. WinUI 3 + .NET 10
itself IS available here — the app and all 8267 unit tests build and pass.

